# Every replaces= and conflicts= entry in a packages/shared/ PKGBUILD, one per line:
# "<package dir> :: <field>=<entry> :: <reason>". [steamling-shared] is in every SoC's repo order,
# so the entry acts on every fleet at once, and replaces= uninstalls on -Syu. check.sh fails on
# an entry without a row and on a row whose entry is gone.
steamling-desktop-kde :: conflicts=steamling-desktop<0.1.0-27 :: files that steamling-desktop shipped before the split
steamling-desktop-kde :: conflicts=steamling-desktop-plasma<0.1.0-1.1 :: /etc/xdg/kwinrc, which steamling-desktop-plasma shipped before it moved here
steamling-desktop-plasma-mobile :: conflicts=steamling-desktop<0.1.0-27 :: files that steamling-desktop shipped before the split
steamling-session :: conflicts=steamling-desktop<0.1.0-27 :: steamos-session-select lived in steamling-desktop before the split
steamling-base-lock :: replaces=mbedtls :: the base renamed mbedtls to mbedtls3 with no conflicts=, so the old copy must go
steamling-base-lock :: conflicts=mbedtls :: pairs the replaces= so the swap survives file collisions
steamling-gamepad-calibration :: replaces=python-pyxel :: retires the GPcal app's runtime
steamling-gamepad-calibration :: conflicts=python-pyxel :: pairs the replaces=
es-de :: conflicts=emulationstation-de :: provides the old name, one ES-DE install at a time
inputplumber :: conflicts=inputplumber :: our build takes the name over ALARM's
wxwidgets-steamling :: conflicts=wxwidgets-common :: provides ALARM's wxwidgets split in one package
wxwidgets-steamling :: conflicts=wxwidgets-gtk3 :: provides ALARM's wxwidgets split in one package
steamling-bsp-common :: conflicts=linux-steamling-sm8550<7.2.10-3 :: the /flash deploy scripts and hook these kernels shipped (#126)
